  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">TZA - Programme de cooperation Tanzania 2023-2028 - Intervention SAKIRP</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZA - Samenwerkingsprogramma Tanzania 2023-2028 - Interventie SAKIRP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAKiRP has constructed 100 bridges on rural feeder roads in the Kigoma region using the stone arch technology. This technology uses local materials and local labour and has significantly lower maintenance costs as well as a longer service life when compared to concrete bridges. The cost reduction of 80% and carbon emission reduction of 75% has convinced the Tanzanian Rural and Urban Roads Agency (TARURA) to incorporate the stone arch technology in its national road development portfolio.
The stone arch technology is new in Tanzania, which means the only capacity amongst engineers and masons is the one built up under SAKiRP in the Kigoma region. To succeed in the national roll out, while maintaining high quality standards, TARURA has requested technical support to help setting up a technical support cell at TARURA HQ and building capacity in the regions selected for phase I of the roll-out.
The stone arch bridges in Kigoma have also been recognized by Enabel as a successful example of the introduction of an appropriate and sustainable construction technology. This is in line with the ambition of Enabel to promote low-carbon, climate-resilient infrastructure and can be used to promote the concept of appropriate technologies in all partner countries.
The name for this transition intervention will be UMARA (Ujenzi wa Madaraja ya Mawe), which means strength in Swahili.
The general objective that was considered under the SAKIRP specific agreement is &#x201c;Local economic development and wellbeing of smallholders is improved in Kigoma Region through sustainable agriculture development&#x201d;. The specific objective to which replies this punctual intervention is &#x201c;Smallholders&#x2019; income is increased and diversified in Kigoma region, especially for women, through pro-poor value chains development&#x201d;
The activities proposed under this phasing-out complement and anchor 3 results considered in the specific agreement: R3: Public and private chain supporters provide effective services to value chains actors; R4: Stronger position of small holders, especially women, in the value chain through improved integration and empowerment and R5: Improved market access and sustainable trade. Local economic development and wellbeing of smallholders is improved in Kigoma Region through sustainable agriculture development: small holders&apos; income is increased and diversified , especially for women through pro-poor value chain development Sustainable Agriculture Kigoma Regional Project - SAKIRP - Phasing out</narrative>
  </description>
